Step 1 — Rewrite `applyCoupon` in src/lib/veloura-store.tsx to call the backend when apiEnabled, fall back to local coupons record when offline.
  The current implementation (line ~55):
  ```ts
  const applyCoupon = useCallback((code: string) => {
    const normalized = code.trim().toUpperCase();
    if (!coupons[normalized]) { toast.error('Invalid or expired coupon.'); return false; }
    setCoupon(normalized); toast.success('Coupon applied successfully'); return true;
  }, []);
  ```
  Replace with an async version. Because applyCoupon is used synchronously in some UI (e.g. CustomerExtras 'Use my 10% off' button), keep the function signature returning `Promise<boolean>` and update all call sites to `.then()`.
  New implementation:
  ```ts
  const applyCoupon = useCallback(async (code: string): Promise<boolean> => {
    const normalized = code.trim().toUpperCase();
    if (apiEnabled) {
      try {
        const result = await api.validateCoupon(normalized, cartSubtotal);
        if (!result.ok) { toast.error(result.error ?? 'Invalid or expired coupon.'); return false; }
        setCoupon(normalized); toast.success('Coupon applied successfully'); return true;
      } catch {
        // Fall through to local validation on network error
      }
    }
    if (!coupons[normalized]) { toast.error('Invalid or expired coupon.'); return false; }
    setCoupon(normalized); toast.success('Coupon applied successfully'); return true;
  }, [cartSubtotal]);
  ```
  Also update the discount calculation: currently `const discount = coupon ? Math.round(cartSubtotal * (coupons[coupon] ?? 0) / 100) : 0;`. This still works correctly — backend validateCoupon returns a discount amount but we only need the code; the store recalculates discount from the local percentage. To also pick up backend-computed discount, store both the coupon code AND the discount percent: add `const [discountPercent, setDiscountPercent] = useState<number>(0)` and set it from the backend response. Then use it in the discount calculation: `const discount = coupon ? Math.round(cartSubtotal * (discountPercent || coupons[coupon] || 0) / 100) : 0;`.

Step 3 — Update the `CheckoutPage` in src/components/veloura/commerce.tsx to use live payment settings from DB.
  - Import `useSettings` from '@/lib/api' (already present in file after FEAT-001).
  - Call `const { data: settingsData } = useSettings();` at the top of `CheckoutPage`.
  - Build available payment methods dynamically:
    ```ts
    const paymentMethods: string[] = [];
    if (settingsData?.payment?.cod_enabled !== false) paymentMethods.push('Cash on Delivery');
    if (settingsData?.payment?.easypaisa_enabled) paymentMethods.push(`EasyPaisa · ${settingsData.payment.easypaisa_number ?? ''}`);
    if (settingsData?.payment?.jazzcash_enabled) paymentMethods.push(`JazzCash · ${settingsData.payment.jazzcash_number ?? ''}`);
    if (settingsData?.payment?.bank_enabled) paymentMethods.push(`Bank Transfer · ${settingsData.payment.bank_name ?? ''}`);
    if (!paymentMethods.length) paymentMethods.push('Cash on Delivery', 'Card — Demo', 'Online Payment — Demo');
    ```
  - Replace the hardcoded `['Cash on Delivery', 'Card — Demo', 'Online Payment — Demo']` array in the payment method selection with `paymentMethods`.
  - If `settingsData?.payment?.payment_note` is set, render it as a `<p>` beneath the payment method selection.
